{
  "description": "Duplicate keep rule: which copy of a duplicate group stays; every other copy is selected for removal. Rules: 'oldest' keeps the earliest creation date (a missing creation date counts as the far future), 'newest' keeps the latest creation date (a missing creation date counts as the far past; the modification date is ignored because Finder/Explorer copies keep it), 'outsideDownloads' keeps the oldest-created copy that is not inside <home>/Downloads (component-aware containment, see path-containment.json), falling back to the oldest of all copies when every copy is in Downloads. Ties on the date go to the shortest path, then ordinal (byte-wise) path order. 'keeper' cases: one group, expected keeper path and expected removal selection (all other paths). 'enforceKeepOne' cases: a hand-edited selection; for every group whose copies are ALL selected, that group's keeper (per rule) is unselected, so one copy per group always stays; everything else in the selection (including paths outside any group) is left as is. Dates are ISO-8601 UTC; null means unknown. Paths use '/'; 'home' is the user's home folder.",
